  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through next Friday) \nIssued at 1020 PM CDT Thu Oct 29 2026\n\nMoisture continues to stream into the area Saturday night and early \nSunday, resulting in high rain chances. Unfortunately, it's still \nnot looking impressive as far as rain amounts with forecast rain \namounts less than one inch. Rain tapers off Sunday evening with \ndrier weather returning for the start of the work week. But by \nTuesday, another low pressure system takes shape to our west. This \nsystem will bring additional rain to Middle TN during the mid-week \nperiod. There's still hope that this system brings more meaningful \nrainfall with still high probabilities of 60-70% of getting at \nleast an inch and a 25-35% chance of some locations picking up \ncloser to two inches. Forecast soundings don't show much in the \nway of instability so thunderstorm potential looks very low.",
